# Encoding — Plan 583 / ISS-48.
#
# Repository text content is UTF-8 WITHOUT a BOM. This is enforced for editors
# and IDEs by .editorconfig (`charset = utf-8`); it is stated here so the
# contract is visible from the file that already governs text handling.
#
# `working-tree-encoding` is deliberately NOT used. It is the one Git
# attribute that would actually enforce encoding, but it re-encodes files on
# checkout: applying it to a tree that contains non-UTF-8 bytes (it did — two
# files were stored as UTF-16LE) silently rewrites them for every contributor
# on their next pull. Fix the tree first, then consider it; do not turn it on
# as a "fix".
#
# The concrete damage encoding drift has already done here: a UTF-8 BOM on the
# first line of a TypeScript file makes any shebang on that line an illegal
# token, which made scripts/__tests__/memory-rag-lib.test.ts fail to load and
# report "no tests" instead of failing. A suite that cannot fail is worse than
# a suite that is red.

# Line ending policy — Plan 550 fixup.

# General policy (2026-09-23, after .git object-store rebuild): normalize
# text files to LF in the repository regardless of each contributor's
# core.autocrlf, so a fresh clone compares equal to any working tree.
*            text=auto

# Windows scripts must keep CRLF (cmd.exe is unreliable with LF).
*.bat        text eol=crlf
*.cmd        text eol=crlf
*.ps1        text eol=crlf

# Binaries: never normalize.
*.png        binary
*.gif        binary
*.jpg        binary
*.jpeg       binary
*.webp       binary
*.ico        binary
*.icns       binary
*.woff       binary
*.woff2      binary
*.ttf        binary
*.zip        binary
*.pdf        binary
*.mp4        binary
*.mp3        binary
*.wav        binary
*.node       binary
*.dll        binary
*.exe        binary
*.sqlite     binary

# Force LF for Handlebars prompt templates regardless of core.autocrlf.
# Force LF for Handlebars prompt templates regardless of core.autocrlf.
# Without this, on Windows checkouts with core.autocrlf=true, every .hbs
# file gets rewritten with CRLF, which then leaks through Handlebars.render
# and breaks byte-level parity tests against the TS source-of-truth. See
# docs/exec-plans/active/550-prompt-hbs-and-agent-decomposition.md for the
# pre-existing failure set this resolves.
*.hbs        text eol=lf
*.md.hbs     text eol=lf